            <ArticleTitle>Orchestration of metabolism by macrophages.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>432-7</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1016/j.cmet.2011.11.013</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Metabolic adaptation is a key component of macrophage plasticity and polarization, instrumental to their function in homeostasis, immunity, and inflammation. Macrophage products also impact metabolism, as illustrated by obesity-associated pathologies. Defining the mechanisms regulating macrophage metabolic activity and orchestration of metabolism by macrophages is crucial to pathology and therapeutic intervention.</AbstractText>
